# Legal & product copy

Follow `docs/architecture/LEGAL_REQUIREMENTS.md`.

- Never claim Helvety can read, decrypt, or recover encrypted content.
- Always state that lost passkeys/recovery keys mean permanent data loss when discussing unlock.
- Do not invent certifications, compliance badges, or “military-grade” fluff.
- Distinguish account data (email, billing metadata) from ciphertext.
- Product legal pack lives under `apps/web/content/legal/` — keep in sync with `CURRENT_POLICY_VERSIONS` (bump versions on material changes).
- Do not reintroduce “NEED SWISS COUNSEL REVIEW” / draft banners on user-facing legal pages (P-legal2 production pack).
- Encryption setup requires acceptance gates for ToS, Privacy, AUP, E2EE ack with version logging.
- Optional Swiss counsel review remains a business risk decision; do not block product copy on it unless the user asks.
